{
  "description": "The proposed works include the addition of a rear extension, previously granted in August 2006 and again in January 2020, while retaining a generous terrace space. The scheme also includes the replacement of the existing terrace doors with new steel‑framed double‑glazed doors to match the existing Crittall‑style windows on the lower floors of the rear elevation, and a relocation of the bedroom to move it away from the noise of Pavilion Road and Basil Street.\nThe site is located on Pavilion Road within the Royal Borough of Kensington and Chelsea, in an area comprising a mix of commercial and residential uses.\nThis application seeks to re‑obtain planning permission for the rear extension, increasing the internal living space. The development respects the existing building materials, and all new materials will match the existing fabric — including a brick wall to the new extension and steel‑framed doors. All drawings illustrating the above will be included within this submission.\nThere is no dedicated on‑site parking, and the surrounding streets are subject to stopping and loading restrictions. The proposed scheme does not require any parking provision. Material deliveries will be scheduled during council‑approved hours. Pedestrian access will not be affected, as all works are confined to the top floor of the building.\nThe rear entrance on Pavilion Road will be used for loading and unloading. The proposed works do not require the use of a crane or any exceptional construction equipment.",
